<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Betwa River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Betwa is a river of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> that rises in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vindhya-range">Vindhya Range</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> and flows north-east for about 590 km to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>. It runs through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> region, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> capital of Orchha was built on an island in its course in 1531.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/betwa-river.jpg" alt="Betwa River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sharvarism · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beautiful_sunset_at_the_Royal_Chhatris_of_Orchha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
